  border: top and bottom rows of both regions are all-bg [observed]
  output: height x W grid = left region with flipped-right non-bg pixels overlaid

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first, then split into left and right halves
  steps:
    1. Choose height H (8-14), half-width W (3-6), separator color (5), 2 fg colors
    2. Build the output grid (H x W) on bg=0 with top/bottom rows all-bg
    3. Place primary color (7-11 pixels) and secondary color (3-5 pixels) as
       sparse foreground, keeping fg fraction 25-40% of H*W
    4. Split output pixels into left-set and right-set (mirrored), allowing 0-6 overlaps
       - each pixel can go to left only, right only, or both
       - ensure each side has at least 5 fg pixels
    5. Assemble input: left region | separator column | fliplr(right region)
    6. Verify separator is unique solid column and colors don't leak across regions
