0022: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0023:     """Fold the grid across its solid vertical separator, overlaying the reflected right side onto the left side.
0024: 
0025:     Input structure
0026:     A non-background vertical separator column spans the full grid height. It
0027:     splits the remaining cells into equal-width left and right regions on the
0028:     background. Reflected foreground overlaps, when present, have the same color.
0029: 
0030:     Rule
0031:     Remove the separator column, mirror the right region horizontally, and
0032:     overlay it onto the left region. For each output pixel, keep the foreground
0033:     color from whichever folded side is non-background; if both sides are
0034:     foreground, their colors must agree.
0035: 
0036:     Key insight
0037:     The two sides are complementary halves around the separator, and the output
0038:     is the separator-free left-side coordinate system after folding the right
0039:     side inward.
